e outcome (0) has overwhelming probability. Lottery A: 0.1% unfavorable, 99.9% favorable. Lottery B: 0.2% unfavorable, 99.8% favorable. So B assigns a greater portion of probability to unfavorable outcomes (0.2% > 0.1%), hence is more right-skewed according to the definition. Therefore, the decision reason, which prefers the lottery that is more right-skewed, prefers Lottery B.",
  "final_answer": "B"
}

